        "original_id": "e9efa5e0-277c-5424-bd65-0ced09863d5a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Rdio, Roku\n- People: Anthony Wood\n- Products: Android, BlackBerry, iOS, Windows Phone, Sonos\n- Concepts: music streaming, offline playback, ad-supported streaming, subscription streaming\n\nFacts:\n- Rdio was an online music streaming service that offered ad-supported free streaming and ad-free subscription streaming in 85 countries.\n- Rdio was available as a website and as an app for Android, BlackBerry, iOS, and Windows Phone devices.\n- Rdio apps could stream music from Rdio's servers or download music for offline playback.\n- Rdio also had clients for the Roku and Sonos systems.\n- Roku was named from the Japanese word 六, pronounced \"roku,\" meaning \"six.\"\n- Roku received its name because it was the sixth company started by Anthony Wood, who served as CEO from 2002 onward.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "75b443ae-80cf-5c63-9961-c0810bfc17f0",
        "text": "Page: Rdio. Sentence: Rdio was an online music streaming service that offered ad-supported free streaming and ad-free subscription streaming services in 85 countries.\nPage: Rdio. Sentence: It was available as a website and via app for Android, BlackBerry, iOS, and Windows Phone mobile devices, which could stream music from Rdio's servers or download music for offline playback; there were also clients for the Roku and Sonos systems.\nPage: Roku. Sentence: The name comes from the Japanese word 六 (roku ) meaning \"six\" and was named so because it was the sixth company that Anthony Wood (CEO 2002-) started.",
